{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-opus-5-5","id":"msg_011CfbK9twj7SmnAjagiRyRJ","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"tool_use","id":"toolu_01CehXvSaCGHZhpeJJzusggb","name":"Bash","input":{"command":"D=/scratch/users/kushinm/auto-psych/outer_loop_live/run1/data/subjective_randomness/experiment2/model_loop/iter_2/candidate_2\ncat << 'EOF' > $D/hypothesis.md\nPeople see a sequence that is built by repeating a short chunk of three or four flips (translational repetition, such as HTTHTTHT or HTTHHTTH) as designed rather than random, so it looks less random by a shared weight on top of the incumbent's judgement (each person's ideal switching rate, personal weights on heads/tails imbalance and on the longest streak, a shared weight on the final streak and on mirror symmetry, and a personal guessing rate). This disagrees most sharply with the current best model on pairs where one sequence repeats a short chunk while having a near-ideal switching rate, good balance and no long streak (e.g. HTHHTHHT or HTTHTTHT against a streakier but non-repeating sequence): the best model calls these sequences highly random, while this model predicts people reject them.\nEOF\necho periodic_chunk_repetition_aversion > $D/model_name.txt\nsed -e '1,9d' /scratch/users/kushinm/auto-psych/outer_loop_live/run1/data/subjective_randomness/experiment2/model_loop/models/mirror_symmetry_streak_aversion_lapse.py > /tmp/body.py\ncat << 'EOF' > $D/candidate.py\n\"\"\"Repetition of a short chunk looks designed, and so less random.\n\nPeople judge a sequence by the incumbent's terms (each person's ideal switching\nrate, personal weights on heads/tails imbalance and the longest streak, shared\nweights on the final streak and on mirror symmetry, a personal guessing rate);\nthe one new mechanism is that a sequence made by repeating a short chunk of\nthree or four flips at least twice over (HTTHTTHT, HTTHHTTH) is recognised as\na pattern and looks less random by a shared weight.\n\"\"\"\nEOF\ncat /tmp/body.py >> $D/candidate.py\ncd $D\npython3 - << 'EOF'\np='candidate.py'; s=open(p).read()\ns=s.replace('''    a = sequence_a.strip().upper()''','''    def periodic(seq):\n        # Smallest period p (partial last repeat allowed); a chunk of 3+ flips\n        # repeated at least twice over the sequence.\n        n = len(seq)\n        for p in range(1, n):\n            if all(seq[i] == seq[i - p] for i in range(p, n)):\n                return 1.0 if 3 <= p and 2 * p <= n else 0.0\n        return 0.0\n\n    a = sequence_a.strip().upper()''')\ns=s.replace('''        \"palin_b\": palindrome(b),\n''','''        \"palin_b\": palindrome(b),\n        \"period_a\": periodic(a),\n        \"period_b\": periodic(b),\n''')\ns=s.replace('''    participant_id = pm.Data(''','''    period_a = pm.Data(\"period_a\", np.zeros(1, dtype=\"float64\"))\n    period_b = pm.Data(\"period_b\", np.zeros(1, dtype=\"float64\"))\n    participant_id = pm.Data(''')\ns=s.replace('''    # Personal lapse''','''    # Shared penalty on repetition of a short chunk (positive: looks designed).\n    omega = pm.Normal(\"omega\", mu=0.0, sigma=1.5)\n\n    # Personal lapse''')\ns=s.replace(\"- rho * palin_a\\n\",\"- rho * palin_a - omega * period_a\\n\")\ns=s.replace(\"- rho * palin_b\\n\",\"- rho * palin_b - omega * period_b\\n\")\nopen(p,'w').write(s)\nEOF\ngrep -n \"omega\\|period\" candidate.py | head -20\ncd /scratch/users/kushinm/auto-psych/outer_loop_live/runs/run1/repo && /scratch/users/kushinm/auto-psych/outer_loop_live/venv/bin/python -m src.pipelines.inner_loop.check_candidate --candidate-dir $D --responses /scratch/users/kushinm/auto-psych/outer_loop_live/run1/data/subjective_randomness/experiment2/model_loop/responses.csv 2>&1 | tail -5"},"caller":{"type":"direct"}}],"container":null,"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":2275,"cache_read_input_tokens":65395,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_token