{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-opus-5-5","id":"msg_011CfbKeF1zYXsdxSyS87xxb","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"I wrote the candidate **`periodic_chunk_repetition_aversion`** and it passes the self-check (`OK`; smoke-fit ELPD-LOO −2335.8). That check doesn't test novelty against the other models, convergence or speed, and it warned about two things:\n\n- **Convergence:** with one chain it can't compute R-hat, so convergence is unverified.\n- **Unreliable LOO estimate:** 8.1% of trials have Pareto k > 0.5, well over the 1% tolerance. I suspect this comes from the short fit and the many person-level parameters, but I haven't checked whether the incumbent shows the same. If it carries into admission's full fit, the model's ELPD will be marked unreliable and it can't be exported as the winner.\n\n**Hypothesis:** A sequence made by repeating a short chunk of three or four flips at least twice (e.g. HTTHTTHT, HTHHTHHT, HTTHHTTH) looks designed, and so less random, by one shared weight. This disagrees most with the current best model on these repeating sequences: they have near-ideal switching, good balance and no long streak, so the best model rates them highly random, while this model predicts people reject them.\n\n**Implementation:** `candidate.py` is the incumbent `mirror_symmetry_streak_aversion_lapse` plus one thing. A new feature flags whether a sequence's smallest repeating unit is 3 or more flips and fits at least twice into its length. Its weight, `omega`, has a Normal(0, 1.5) prior. Every other term is unchanged.\n\n**Why this mechanism:** About 20 of the 128 stimulus pairs contain such a sequence. In several, the repeating sequence is chosen surprisingly rarely: HTHHTHHT is picked over HTHTTHTH only 30% of the time, and HTTHTTHT over HTHTHHHH 33% of the time.\n\n**Things to know:**\n- **Not aimed at the critique:** The one discrepancy it reported (people differ more in consistency than the model produces) didn't survive the FDR correction (q = 0.21). I chose a structural mechanism instead, so this model doesn't address it.\n- **Possible novelty failure:** Some repeating sequences are also palindromes (HTTHHTTH, THHTTHHT), which the incumbent already penalises. The new term only adds information on the non-palindromic ones, so it could fall under the 0.002 novelty threshold if `omega` comes out near zero.\n\nAll three files are in `/scratch/users/kushinm/auto-psych/outer_loop_live/run1/data/subjective_randomness/experiment2/model_loop/iter_2/candidate_2/`: `hypothesis.md`, `model_name.txt` and `candidate.py`."}],"container":null,"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":2470,"cache_read_input_tokens":70693,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":2470,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":0},"output_tokens":8,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"global"},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"13f60187-88bd-4f38-9df9-87cdbaef827d","uuid":"7a0ea559-e90a-4785-b92a-7208dc1aa7a0","timestamp":"2026-10-01T10:00:17.724Z","request_id":"req_011CfbKeETFpPgJYdqgecUjQ"}
